---
import LegalPage from '@/components/legal/legal-page.astro'
import LegalSection from '@/components/legal/legal-section.astro'
import { legalUpdated } from '@/lib/legal'
import { externalLinks, support } from '@/lib/links'
---

<LegalPage
  description="Treid's privacy policy: what the hosted Treid stores, what stays at Alpaca, what stays in your browser and how to delete your data."
  title="Privacy policy"
  updated={legalUpdated['/privacy']}
>
  <LegalSection title="Scope">
    <p>
      <strong>Treid requires your own Alpaca account.</strong> Alpaca is your broker and holds your
      money and trading data. Treid connects to it with the API keys you add.
    </p>
    <p>
      Treid is the infrastructure in between. It gives you the screens and the server to use what
      Alpaca does, and workspaces so a team can trade together. It only stores what it needs to do
      that, listed below.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page covers the hosted Treid on this site. Treid is open source, so other people run
      their own copies. If you sign in to someone else's copy, they hold your data, not us.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="What we store">
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account:</strong> your name, email address, whether you verified it, and a scrypt hash
        of your password. If you sign in with Google, we also store the Google account link, the
        access, refresh and ID tokens Google issues with the scopes you granted, and your Google
        profile photo URL.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Profile photo:</strong> the PNG, JPEG or WebP photo you add at sign-up, up to 90 KB,
        stored in the database.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Workspaces:</strong> each workspace's name, its members and their roles, and pending
        invitations with the invited email address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Alpaca connections:</strong> the API key ID and secret for each connection, encrypted
        with AES-256-GCM, plus its name, paper or live, and the last 4 characters of the key ID so you
        can tell connections apart.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Order history:</strong> every order placed through Treid, with who placed it,
        through which connection, the symbol, side, quantity or amount, prices and status, and when it
        was replaced or canceled.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Activity log:</strong> bulk cancels, closed positions, connection changes, member and
        role changes, deposit address changes and workspace switches, with who made each one.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deposit addresses:</strong> the USDC and USDT addresses you save for Ethereum and
        Solana.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sessions:</strong> for each signed-in session, the IP address and browser user agent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email links:</strong> a one-time token for each email verification and password reset
        link, with your email address, kept until it is used or expires.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rate limits:</strong> counts of recent sign-in attempts per IP address, to block
        password guessing, and of recent Alpaca key changes per account.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="What stays at Alpaca">
    <p>
      Your balance, positions, orders, watchlists and account details live in your Alpaca account.
      Treid fetches them from Alpaca with your keys when you open a page. We don't keep a copy,
      except the order history described above. Alpaca's own <a href={externalLinks.alpaca}
        >privacy policy</a
      > covers what Alpaca does with your data.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="What stays in your browser">
    <ul>
      <li>A secure session cookie that keeps you signed in.</li>
      <li>Your theme, your chart type and your chart zoom, saved in local storage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      That's all. The app has no analytics, no ads and no tracking scripts. This site counts page
      views with Vercel Web Analytics, which is anonymous and sets no cookies.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="Who else is involved">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Alpaca</strong> receives every request Treid makes with your keys.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong>, only if you sign in with Google.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Resend</strong> sends the verification, password reset and invitation emails, so it
        sees your email address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our hosting and database providers</strong> run the app and store the data above.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Parqet</strong> serves the company and fund logos. In the app, our server fetches
        them through its image proxy, so Parqet sees our server and the symbols shown, not your IP
        address. On this site, your browser loads them straight from Parqet, so Parqet sees your IP
        address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>randomuser.me</strong> serves the sample profile photos on this site's home page.
        Your browser loads them straight from randomuser.me, so it sees your IP address.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell your data or share it with anyone else, unless the law makes us.</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="Who in your workspace sees what">
    <p>
      Members of a workspace see its members, roles, connection names, order history and activity
      log. They never see your password or the keys themselves. Connections belong to the workspace,
      so keys you add stay there when you leave.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="Deleting your data">
    <ul>
      <li>Removing a connection deletes its encrypted keys.</li>
      <li>
        Deleting a workspace deletes its connections, order history, activity log and invitations.
      </li>
      <li>You can remove a saved deposit address at any time.</li>
      <li>
        There's no delete button for the account yet. Email <a href={support.href}>{support.email}</a>{' '}
        from your account's address and we'll delete it, along with your photo, sessions and deposit
        addresses.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Orders and activity you made in a workspace you didn't own stay in that workspace's history,
      but your name is removed from them. Invitation entries keep the email address that was
      invited.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="Security">
    <p>
      Keys are encrypted before they reach the database and are only decrypted on the server to call
      Alpaca. They are never sent to your browser. The code is <a href={externalLinks.github}
        >public on GitHub</a
      >, so you can check this yourself. To report a security problem, email <a href={support.href}
        >{support.email}</a
      > instead of opening a public issue.
    </p>
    <p>
      Encryption protects the keys we store, not copies kept anywhere else. Keeping your keys and
      secrets private is up to you, on this site and on a copy you host yourself. If you run your own
      copy, you hold the database and the encryption keys, so its security is yours to manage. If a
      key may have leaked, revoke it in Alpaca and add a new one.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection title="Changes">
    <p>
      When this page changes, the date at the top changes too. We'll email you before any change to
      what we store or who we share it with.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>
</LegalPage>
